**(i) Popular name of the Constitution (1 mark).** The **Federal Constitution** (the Constitution of the Federal Republic of Cameroon of 1961), also called the Foumban Constitution after the Foumban Constitutional Conference of July 1961 where its draft was discussed.

**(ii) Month and year it came into effect (2 marks).** **October 1961** (1 October 1961, the day of the reunification of the two Cameroons, when the Federal Republic of Cameroon was born). The extract says that Ahidjo signed it into law on 1 September 1961; it took effect one month later.

**(iii) Two functions of the President as Head of State and Head of Government (2 marks).** Any two of the following (1 mark each):
- he was the **head of the executive**: he appointed the Vice-President (who came from West Cameroon) and the federal ministers and directed the government;
- he was **commander-in-chief of the armed forces**;
- he **promulgated the laws** passed by the Federal Assembly and could legislate by **ordinances** when the Assembly was not sitting;
- he **represented the Federal Republic** abroad, signed treaties and accredited ambassadors;
- he appointed the top civil servants and judges and had the right of pardon.
